(Use cases for the campus bike-share system) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Actors: Rider, Station Operator, Payment Service \(external\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Rent a bike - primary actor Rider.) Tj T*
(Main flow: 1. The Rider selects a station in the app. 2. The system lists the bikes at) Tj T*
(that station with their battery level. 3. The Rider reserves a bike. 4. The system holds) Tj T*
(it for ten minutes. 5. The Rider unlocks it with the app and the rental starts.) Tj T*
(Alternative flows: 4a. The Rider does not arrive in ten minutes: the hold is released.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Rebalance stations - primary actor Station Operator.) Tj T*
(Main flow: 1. The Operator opens the map of stations. 2. The system highlights stations) Tj T*
(that are empty or full. 3. The Operator moves bikes and confirms each move. 4. The system) Tj T*
(updates the counts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pay a monthly pass - primary actor Rider, supporting actor Payment Service.) Tj T*
(Main flow: 1. The Rider chooses a monthly pass. 2. The system sends the amount to the) Tj T*
(Payment Service. 3. The Payment Service confirms. 4. The system activates the pass.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
